window.docContents[187].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Pull":{"contents":"Body A of pair P wobbles instead of sliding along the line. Its centre of mass is off the springs' line of action, so the spring force misses the centre of mass, produces a torque, and rotates the body. Body A therefore stops being a point mass: it opens into left and right halves, acquires a mass distribution and inertia tensor, and needs a body-fixed frame beside the lab frame. One name remains one system: records under that name are its states at different times, configurations, or rival estimates; comparing them is the point. Distinct names are distinct systems. HalfOf .P .A keeps body A's halves shared across descriptions of pair P, while a half of pair Q has a different bearer type.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L3 — The body opens up","header":"5.4.3. Pull","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Pull"}});